  "initial_review": "Complete normalized comparison: 22 non-exclusion or mixed structural chunks and 54 pure exclusion chunks. Mixed #error/SAS branch rewrites are included in register, not hidden as exclusions.",
  "counter_review": "BIOS mode selects caller aperture; current global display may belong to another virtual context. SAS performs translation, unlike raw host pointer writes or host scrolling. Keep this ownership separation. Build generator deliberately selects MONITOR/X86GFX only for video.c NTIO setup, so globally disabling MONITOR is not an equivalent simplification. Three scalar write routes reuse original SAS operations but duplicate/rearrange original alternatives inconsistently; simplify their conditional expression/placement together while preserving original outer frame and selected NTIO path.",
  "evidence": "video.c:231 mode table mono B0000/B7FFF and colour B8000/BFFFF; :814/:965/:1186/:1318 scroll origins; :1042-1044 matching upper bound; :1595-1624/:1683-1706/:2185-2208 scalar SAS selections. tools/build/New-T310OriginalSoftpcNinja.ps1:983-997 per-TU flags. ccpusas4.c:1007 move through c_sas_hw_at/c_sas_store, translation paths use xtrn2phy. ega_vide.c:2105 void ega_read_dot(int,int,int).",
  "limits": "Functional remediation not applied; no new build or runtime validation."
